# T-1101: TypeAlias constraint enforcement at instantiation time.
# SortKey is a parameterized type alias whose parameter carries a @Comparable constraint.
# Using SortKey with Int is valid — Int has a Comparable instance in the prelude.
# The constraint is checked during alias instantiation in instantiate_type_alias.
# Absence of === warn asserts no type errors: the constraint is satisfied cleanly.
[
  SortKey: [type [let a@Comparable] a]

  # Annotate a function parameter with SortKey instantiated at Int.
  # Int satisfies Comparable (ComparableInt instance in prelude), so instantiation succeeds.
  identity-key: [fn@Integer [let k@[SortKey Int]] k]

  result: [identity-key 42]
]
=== out
["SortKey": []  "identity-key": [fn [let k] ...]  "result": 42]
